  ('growing-older-gently', 1, 'Name one skill you have now that you did not have ten years ago, and say it out loud.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 2, 'Stretch slowly beside your bed this morning and notice which parts of you have carried you the longest.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 3, 'Ask someone older than you what they wish they had known at your age, and write down one phrase from their answer.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 4, 'Catch the next time you say "I''m too old for that" and try "I haven''t tried that yet" instead.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 5, 'Write down three things you still want to do in your life, big or small, and keep the list somewhere you will see it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 6, 'Write down a lesson you learned the hard way, and thank the younger you who paid for it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 7, 'Look at your most comfortable shoes and thank them for the miles they have walked with you over the years.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 8, 'Call a grandparent, aunt, uncle or older family friend and find out what an ordinary Saturday looked like when they were your age.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 9, 'Write down one sentence you often say about your age, then rewrite it the way a kind friend would say it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 10, 'Start a "someday" list on a fresh page and add the first thing that comes to mind.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 11, 'Pick a memory you are glad to carry and spend two quiet minutes with it over your morning coffee.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 12, 'Move a brighter lamp to the chair where you read, because eyes that have read for years deserve good light.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 13, 'Teach someone younger a skill you learned the slow way, like folding a fitted sheet or reading a paper map.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 14, 'Greet your reflection this morning the way you would greet an old friend at the door.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 15, 'Pick one small thing to look forward to next season and put it on your calendar.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 16, 'Think of a problem you handled recently and notice how differently you would have handled it years back.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 17, 'Book a routine checkup today, just the booking, as a kind promise to the body that has come this far with you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 18, 'Text a former teacher or coach a short note about one thing they said that stayed with you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 19, 'Read the jokes in a birthday card aisle for a minute and notice which ones sting and which ones feel warm.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 20, 'Look up one class near you or online that sounds fun, and read its description slowly.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 21, 'List three friends who shaped who you are, and add one word for what each one gave you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 22, 'Take the stairs at whatever pace feels right today, and let all the years behind you set an unhurried rhythm.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 23, 'Learn one piece of slang from a teenager, and let them explain exactly when it is used.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 24, 'Choose a birthday card that celebrates the person rather than teasing them about the number.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 25, 'Sign up for a class you have been curious about, even a single evening session.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 26, 'Find an old photo of yourself and look at it the way you would look at a dear friend''s picture.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 27, 'Rest for ten minutes this afternoon without apologizing, the way you would let a longtime friend sit down.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 28, 'Invite a younger friend or relative to show you a phone game they love, and play one round together.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 29, 'Notice one age joke on TV tonight and ask yourself, quietly, whether you actually agree with it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 30, 'Draft a short letter to yourself ten years from now, telling future you what you hope they still enjoy.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 31, 'Tell someone a short story from your past that only you could tell.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 32, 'Run a warm bath this evening and let the water soften shoulders that have held years of worry and work.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 33, 'Cook a family recipe with someone from another generation, and let them hold the spoon for the tricky part.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 34, 'Say "hello, you" to a new gray hair when you find one, and leave it be.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 35, 'Jot down a family recipe you want to pass on, with the little tips you usually only say out loud.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 36, 'Notice one thing you used to worry about that barely crosses your mind now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 37, 'Pick one piece of clothing today simply because you feel good in it at the age you are right now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 38, 'Look up a local group that mixes ages, such as a choir, garden club or book circle, and save the next meeting time.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 39, 'Touch a laugh line by your eye and name one thing that made you laugh hard enough to earn it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 40, 'Notice one moment today that made you feel useful, and name it to yourself before bed.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 41, 'On your commute, recall a place that shaped you and picture its sounds and smells.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 42, 'Place a hand on your heart tonight and thank your body for every year of steady work it has done for you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 43, 'Tell a younger coworker about a mistake that taught you something, keeping the story light and short.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 44, 'Plan one way to mark your next birthday that involves no apology for the number.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 45, 'Ask yourself what kind of older person you hope to become, then do one small thing that fits that picture.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 46, 'Jot down a phrase you say often and remember who you picked it up from.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 47, 'Think of a hobby you love and make one small change so it still fits the body you have this year.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 48, 'Name one person older than you who seems to be living fully, and write down what you admire about how they do it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 49, 'Practice saying your age out loud in a calm, plain voice, the way you would say your street name.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 50, 'Try something today you have never done before, like a new route on your walk or a new dish at lunch.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 51, 'Cook a dish you learned to make along the way and remember who first showed you how.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 52, 'Schedule an eye exam if one is due, and let making the call be enough kindness for today.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 53, 'Copy down a recipe exactly as an elder makes it, including every "pinch of this" and "until it looks right."'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 54, 'Swap "back when I was young" for "back when I was learning" the next time you tell a story.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 55, 'Tell a friend about one thing you plan to explore this year and notice how it feels to say it aloud.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 56, 'Look at your hands while washing dishes and name three things they have learned to do.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 57, 'Roll your shoulders gently three times while the kettle heats, and stop if anything pinches or hurts.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 58, 'Sit with an older neighbor on the porch for a few minutes this evening and hear how the street has changed.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 59, 'Look at an old photo of yourself and say one kind thing to that person, then one to the person holding it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 60, 'Record a short voice memo of a story from your life you would like someone to hear one day.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 61, 'Send a short note to an old friend telling them one thing they taught you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 62, 'Notice how your hands have changed over the years and name one thing they have made or held that you cherish.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 63, 'Play a song from your teenage years for someone younger, and trade it for one of their favorites.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 64, 'Skip comparing your energy to your younger self for one afternoon, and notice what this energy is good for.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 65, 'Add one place you would love to visit to your someday list, even if it is just across town.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 66, 'Ask yourself what you know about kindness now that you did not know as a teenager.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 67, 'Sit down to put on your socks this morning if that feels easier, and call it wisdom you have gathered with time.'),
