  ('growing-older-gently', 252, 'Warm your hands around a mug on a chilly morning and let the heat ease fingers that have worked for years.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 253, 'Read about a mentoring program at work or in your community, and what it asks of volunteers.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 254, 'Turn your birthday candles into a list of favorite moments, one memory for each candle you can recall.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 255, 'Cross one tiny item off your someday list today, or shrink it until it fits into this week.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 256, 'Appreciate one way your taste has changed, in food, music or clothes, and enjoy who you are now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 257, 'Plan a short nap or a quiet sit for later today and protect it like any other appointment your older self would keep.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 258, 'Swap a recipe with a friend from a different generation, and cook theirs soon.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 259, 'Sit outside on a summer evening and name three things you appreciate more now than you once did.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 260, 'Play a song you have never heard before from a style you usually skip, and listen all the way to the end.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 261, 'Remember a teacher, coach or neighbor who believed in you and write their name somewhere you will see it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 262, 'Check that the hallway and stairs at home are well lit, and change one dim bulb for a brighter one for the years ahead.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 263, 'Talk with your oldest friend about how you have each changed since you met.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 264, 'Collect the kindest phrase you hear about growing older today and repeat it to yourself before bed.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 265, 'Consider what advice your older self might give you today, and follow one part of it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 266, 'Explain to yourself, in a sentence or two, how you now know when to ask for help.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 267, 'Ease into your morning by sitting on the edge of the bed for a few breaths before you stand.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 268, 'Jot down the names of older people who made your childhood better, and say a quiet thank you for each.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 269, 'Look at a spring tree as it moves from blossom to leaf, and notice that each stage has its own beauty.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 270, 'Reserve a free spot at a talk, concert or library event coming up later this season.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 271, 'Catch one moment at work today when an old worry no longer pulls at you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 272, 'Write a short thank you note to your body, as if to a friend who has stayed with you through every birthday.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 273, 'Think of an elder you lost touch with, and look for a simple way to say hello soon.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 274, 'Gather a few fallen autumn leaves and admire the colors that only arrive late in the season.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 275, 'Bake or cook something from a recipe you saved long ago but never tried.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 276, 'Pause at lunch and name something you understand about people that took years to learn.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 277, 'Learn a gentler version of a pastime you love, like a shorter walking route or a lighter racket, so it stays yours for years.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 278, 'Offer to learn something alongside a young person in your family, whatever they are curious about right now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 279, 'Give your birthday a full sentence of welcome in your journal, starting with "I''m glad to be..."'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 280, 'Over coffee or tea, sketch a rough plan for one small project you could finish by next season.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 281, 'Keep a slip of paper in your pocket and add each small skill you notice yourself using today.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 282, 'Leave the dishes for a moment and stretch your back against the counter, slowly, stopping before anything aches.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 283, 'Pass a family story to a younger relative so it keeps traveling forward.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 284, 'Retire one phrase about your body''s age that you say on autopilot, and pick a gentler one to use.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 285, 'Describe in a few sentences how you would like to spend an ordinary afternoon many years from now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 286, 'Revisit a hobby you once loved for ten minutes, just to see what your hands remember.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 287, 'Carry a lighter bag today by taking out one thing you do not need, and let shoulders that have hauled plenty for years enjoy the break.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 288, 'Visit a farmers market and chat with a vendor from a different generation about how they learned their craft.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 289, 'Stop yourself before saying "you don''t look your age" to someone, and try "you look happy" instead.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 290, 'Volunteer an hour of your time, or look up one local place that welcomes helpers.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 291, 'Tell a young person in your life a true story about a time you got something wrong and what came of it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 292, 'Borrow a large print book or an audiobook from the library and enjoy a story without straining your eyes.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 293, 'Check in with an older person you trust about how they make new friends these days.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 294, 'Leave the "I''ll never tell my age" joke out of your next introduction, and enjoy the plainness of the truth.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 295, 'Pause before dinner and ask yourself, "What am I looking forward to?" and let any answer count.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 296, 'Wonder which of your current habits your younger self would be surprised by, and enjoy the surprise.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 297, 'Put a favorite cushion on your seat at work, a small comfort for a body that has sat through many meetings.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 298, 'Volunteer to explain an old family tradition to the newest member of the family.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 299, 'Hold your hands in good light and thank them for all the things they have carried and made.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 300, 'Read about someone who started something new later in life and note what you admire in them.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 301, 'Light a candle or lamp this evening and spend a moment with a memory you are thankful for.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 302, 'Unclench your jaw and drop your shoulders while you wait in line, a small kindness for a body that has waited in many lines.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 303, 'Start a word game over text with a relative much older or much younger than you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 304, 'Share one thing you have stopped worrying about since you were younger with someone you trust.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 305, 'Swap part of your usual evening routine for one new small activity, like a crossword or a quick sketch.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 306, 'Smell something familiar, cinnamon, cut grass or soap, and follow the memory it brings back.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 307, 'Sit in the sun for a few minutes on a cool spring day and let your joints enjoy the warmth.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 308, 'At a school concert or recital, say hello to a grandparent sitting nearby and learn which performer is theirs.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 309, 'Recall an age you once dreaded and list one good thing that happened when you got there.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 310, 'Hang or tape your someday list somewhere you pass each morning.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 311, 'Address a short thank you note to a place, a town, a school or a kitchen, that helped make you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 312, 'Hum a song while you stretch your calves against a wall, slowly and gently, and stop if anything hurts.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 313, 'Invite an older relative to pass on a skill they would hate to see forgotten, and set a time to learn it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 314, 'Admire one older character in a show or film who is lively, wise or funny, and say out loud why.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 315, 'Leave a kind note for a future you inside a coat pocket you will wear next winter.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 316, 'Admire a worn object you own, a mug, a jacket, a tool, as a record of years you have lived well.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 317, 'Notice one moment today when you moved more carefully than you once did, and thank yourself for that wisdom.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 318, 'Teach a young adult something practical you wish someone had shown you, like how to read a lease.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 319, 'Question one "act your age" rule you follow, and let yourself wear the bright color or dance in the kitchen anyway.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 320, 'In the spring, walk somewhere green and choose one thing you would like to do there again next year.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 321, 'Ask yourself what you no longer need to prove, and let that feel like a gift.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 322, 'Lay out comfortable clothes tonight for tomorrow, choosing what feels kind on your skin at this stage of life.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 323, 'Read an interview or memoir by someone older than you who is still trying new things.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 324, 'Picture yourself many years from now reading today''s journal page, and write one line you think they would love to find.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 325, 'Collect three pieces of wisdom from people in your life and write them where you can return to them.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 326, 'Hold a warm cup of tea and think of the friend who knows you best and how long that took to build.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 327, 'Use both hands to carry the laundry basket today, and let carefulness be a quiet form of respect for your years.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 328, 'Learn the name of one elder on your street or in your building whom you have not met yet.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 329, 'Read your birthday messages slowly and let each kind word land without deflecting it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 330, 'Text someone you would like to spend time with soon and suggest a simple plan.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 331, 'Sort one drawer of keepsakes and keep out the item that tells the best story.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 332, 'Share with a friend one way you have made your daily routine more comfortable as the years have gone by.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 333, 'Let a younger relative help you set up something new on your phone, and thank them for their patience.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 334, 'Breathe in while thinking "another year," and breathe out while thinking "another chance to be me."'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 335, 'Look ahead to the next holiday or gathering and decide on one small way to make it your own.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 336, 'Imagine your younger self watching you go about today, and notice what would impress them.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 337, 'Enjoy a slow cup of tea after a winter walk and let your body warm up at its own pace.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 338, 'Tell someone older which of their skills you would love to have one day.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 339, 'Write your age on a sticky note followed by three things you love about this year of your life.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 340, 'Finish the sentence "Lately I am becoming someone who" in your journal, and let the ending be hopeful.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 341, 'Mark the next time you stay calm in a frustrating moment and quietly credit the years for it.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 342, 'Note the date of your last eye exam or checkup on a sticky note so booking the next one feels simple.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 343, 'Watch an older relative knit, bake or fix something for a while, and ask what they think about as they work.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 344, 'Give a cheerful answer the next time a coworker teases you about your age, such as "and I''ve enjoyed every year."'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 345, 'Practice saying yes to one small invitation or idea today that you might usually turn down.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 346, 'Trace the path that led you to someone you love, and appreciate each small turn along the way.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 347, 'Pick a jar opener, a garden glove or another small tool that makes an everyday job easier on your hands.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 348, 'Share a funny story from your own younger years with someone who is in that same stage now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 349, 'Let yourself be the oldest person in a room without shrinking, and notice what you contribute.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 350, 'Revisit a goal you set aside years ago and ask whether a smaller version of it could fit your life now.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 351, 'Celebrate one hard season you came through by naming one thing it gave you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 352, 'Celebrate one ordinary thing your body did today, like getting out of bed or tying a shoe, as a quiet gift from your years.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 353, 'Before bed, recall one person older than you who showed you that growing up keeps going, and let it comfort you.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 354, 'Remember a time someone older surprised you by trying something new, and borrow a bit of their nerve.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 355, 'Wear something a little different today, a color or style you have been curious to try.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 356, 'Leave a voice message for yourself describing a memory you never want to lose.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 357, 'Fold a soft towel under your neck tonight if your sleep has changed over the years, and see what feels kind.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 358, 'Find out what a grandparent or older friend is curious about these days, and share one curiosity of yours.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 359, 'Ask someone younger than you what they hope to keep doing for a very long time, and share your own answer.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 360, 'During a winter evening indoors, list three things you hope to do once the days grow longer.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 361, 'Settle into a comfortable chair and ask what you would miss if the years had not added up, then savor the answer.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 362, 'Offer yourself the same patience you would give a beloved elder as you move through your day, whatever your age.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 363, 'Write a short note to your younger self from the person you are today, then one to your older self too.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 364, 'Celebrate the plain fact of another birthday by eating your favorite breakfast slowly and without a single apology.'),
  ('growing-older-gently', 365, 'End the day by writing one sentence about what gave it meaning, and one thing you hope tomorrow holds.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
